id: pm-xmmafu
title: "A block-enforced ratchet ceiling stops resolving when its population reaches zero, so the gate fails with an unhandled error on the day the remediation it enforces succeeds"
description: "A ratchet ceiling exists to drive a defect population to zero. One of the five validation ceilings this project enforces reads its observation from a key that the producer discards when the population reaches zero, so the gate stops evaluating on the day the remediation it enforces succeeds, and it fails with an unhandled error rather than a verdict.\n\n## How this was found\n\nNot by inspection. By doing the remediation.\n\nFour active items were missing estimated_minutes. I backfilled all four, which took the population from 4 to 0, and then declared the missing ceiling as data so the class could not regrow. The gate refused to run:\n\n    pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci --dry-run\n      exit 1\n      code    \"unknown_error\"\n      title   \"Unhandled error\"\n      detail  \"assurance field counts.missing_estimated_minutes must resolve\n               to a finite number or string array\"\n      required \"Inspect command input and runtime state, then retry.\"\n\nThe field had resolved fine ten minutes earlier, when the value was 4.\n\n## The mechanism\n\nsrc/sdk/governance/validate.ts:1302 buildMetadataCounts:\n\n    for (const field of metadataPolicy.required_fields) {\n      const missing = missingByField[field];\n      const value = missing ? missing.length : 0;\n      const countKey = METADATA_COUNT_KEY_BY_FIELD[field];\n      if (value > 0 && countKey) {\n        counts[countKey] = value;\n      }\n    }\n\nThe zero is computed on the line above and then deliberately not emitted. Absent and zero are the same byte sequence to any consumer, which is pm-b1w8vr's content-conditional projection defect, here on the validation surface and with an enforcement consumer attached.\n\n## Scope, measured rather than assumed\n\nThe guard is not project-wide. Seventeen zero-valued count keys are emitted unconditionally across eight validation checks, including lifecycle.dependency_cycle_count, dependency_references.dangling_reference_count, files.pm_internal_excluded_count, history_drift.drifted_items_count, format_version.outdated_items_count and storage_integrity.pending_merge_decision_count. Those are all safe and their assertions will keep resolving at zero.\n\nExactly one sub-object applies the guard: metadata.counts. It has exactly two members, missing_estimated_minutes and closed_missing_close_reason.\n\nExactly one live gate assertion sources a member of it:\n\n    validate-missing-close-reason-ceiling\n      measurement source  validate  check metadata  field counts.closed_missing_close_reason\n      ceiling             16\n      enforcement         block\n      gate                tracker-context-quality  triggers ci, pre-release\n\nSixteen closed items are missing a close reason. pm-e9zh and pm-wenq exist to finish exactly that backfill. When they do, this happens:\n\n    16 -> 0\n    counts.closed_missing_close_reason disappears from the envelope\n    the measurement cannot resolve\n    the gate exits 1 with unknown_error on every ci and pre-release trigger\n\nThe gate breaks when its own remediation completes. It is one item away, and the failure it produces names neither the assertion, nor the measurement, nor the reason, and advises the operator to inspect runtime state and retry.\n\n## Why the obvious alternative source does not work either\n\nThe natural second encoding is an items measurement filtering on the field being unset. That path is already known broken: pm-py7qv2 owns the finding that an items source with equals null silently matches nothing, verified against a release truth of 655 returning 0. So today there is no working way to declare either of these two populations as data. One source vanishes at zero and the other cannot express null. That is why this item is ordered behind py7qv2 rather than proposing a workaround.\n\n## Disposition taken in this session\n\nThe estimate backfill is kept: four items now carry estimates and the validate_metadata_missing_estimate warning is gone, which is correct work independent of this defect.\n\nThe declaration is withdrawn. validate-missing-estimate-ceiling and its measurement were created, proved unsatisfiable, unwired from the gate and removed. tracker-context-quality is back to forty assertions and passes. The withdrawal is recorded here rather than left as a silent revert, because the attempt is the evidence.\n\n## Why a bound whose polarity is a ceiling of zero is the general case\n\nThis is not specific to two fields. Any ceiling whose target is zero is, by construction, a bound whose satisfying state is the state its own observation must survive. A producer that treats zero as absence makes every such bound self-defeating. The rule the fix should adopt is the inverse of the current guard: a count that a contract declares is emitted whenever the contract applies, and its value at zero is zero."
