author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A validation count that a check declares is emitted whenever that check runs, carrying the value zero rather than being omitted, so absence of a key means the contract does not apply and never means the population is empty; Every assurance measurement whose bound is a ceiling of zero is proven to resolve while the bound holds, by a negative control that evaluates the measurement against a population of exactly zero; An assurance measurement whose source field cannot be resolved fails with a typed refusal naming the gate, the assertion, the measurement and the unresolved field, and never as an unhandled error advising the operator to retry; The close-reason ceiling survives its own remediation: a regression test drives the closed-missing-close-reason population to zero and asserts the gate returns a pass verdict rather than an error"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: critical
confidence: 95
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Declared zero-valued counts remain resolvable and unresolved assurance sources identify the complete gate/assertion/measurement/source location.
actual_result: "Zero close-reason populations pass; missing fields return a typed refusal with gate, assertion, measurement, source kind, check, and field; exact repository coverage is 100/100/100/100."
